counterfactuals.output:
Applying the revised Expanding Photosphere Method—using improved atmosphere-model dilution factors and photospheric velocities—to Type II-P supernovae largely removes the distance underestimate found with older EPM implementations. Comparisons with distances from Type Ia supernovae show:

- no statistically significant systematic offset in the distance scale;
- mean distances consistent with the Type Ia scale to roughly the 5–10% level;
- individual Type II-P distances typically accurate to about 10–20%, with larger scatter than standardized Type Ia measurements.

Thus, revised EPM provides an independent and broadly unbiased extragalactic distance indicator, although its precision is still limited by atmosphere models, extinction, explosion-time estimates, and departures from spherical symmetry.
